        "original_id": "426b5679-9ca7-591a-908f-c3c5782aac86",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Sanders–Brown Center on Aging, Eleanor and John Y. Brown Jr. Foundation\n- People: John Y. Brown Jr.\n- Roles: Governor of Kentucky\n- Companies: Kentucky Fried Chicken (KFC)\n\nFacts:\n- In 1972, a grant from the Eleanor and John Y. Brown Jr. Foundation led to the construction of the current Sanders–Brown Center on Aging facility.\n- From 1979 to 1983, John Y. Brown Jr. served as the 55th governor of Kentucky.\n- John Y. Brown Jr. is also known for building Kentucky Fried Chicken into a multimillion-dollar restaurant chain.",
